# Phase 2 — Monitor CRUD + Scheduler + Pinger Engine

## Goal
Wire up the APScheduler pinger engine so that monitors are pinged on their configured interval, results are written to `check_logs`, and monitor status (`up`/`down`) is kept current. All scheduler lifecycle hooks (start, register on create, cancel on delete/pause, resume on restart) must be in place.

**What's already done (Phase 1 leftovers):**
- All ORM models exist: `Monitor`, `CheckLog`, `AlertChannel`
- `ping_url()` in [`monitors/service.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/monitors/service.py) — fully implemented ✅
- `send_alerts()` + channel senders in [`alerts/service.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/alerts/service.py) — fully implemented ✅
- Monitor CRUD router in [`monitors/router.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/monitors/router.py) — stub (no scheduler calls yet) ⚠️
- Logs router in [`logs/router.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/logs/router.py) — only `GET /logs`, missing `/logs/stats` ⚠️
- `scheduler.py` — **does not exist yet** ❌
- `main.py` — no lifespan, no scheduler start/stop ❌
- `AsyncSessionLocal` already exported from [`database.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/database.py) ✅

