### Component 3 — Monitor Router (add scheduler hooks)

#### [MODIFY] [`monitors/router.py`](file:///d:/MonitoringEngine/app/monitors/router.py)

Four endpoints need scheduler integration:

| Endpoint | Change |
|---|---|
| `POST /api/monitors` | After commit, call `add_monitor_job(id, interval)` |
| `DELETE /api/monitors/{id}` | Before delete, call `remove_monitor_job(id)` |
| `POST /api/monitors/{id}/pause` | After setting `is_active=False`, call `remove_monitor_job(id)` |
| `POST /api/monitors/{id}/resume` | After setting `is_active=True`, call `add_monitor_job(id, interval)` |

```python
# Add import at top:
from app.monitors.scheduler import add_monitor_job, remove_monitor_job

# create_monitor — add after await db.refresh(monitor):
add_monitor_job(str(monitor.id), monitor.interval_minutes)

# delete_monitor — add before await db.delete(monitor):
remove_monitor_job(str(monitor_id))

# pause_monitor — add after await db.commit():
remove_monitor_job(str(monitor_id))

# resume_monitor — add after await db.refresh(monitor):
add_monitor_job(str(monitor.id), monitor.interval_minutes)
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> `update_monitor` also needs consideration: if `interval_minutes` is changed, the existing job must be re-registered with the new interval. Add a call to `add_monitor_job()` after the update commit if `interval_minutes` is in the updated fields.

